      "id": "seg:paragraph:discussion:0008:0001",
      "blockId": "paragraph:discussion:0008",
      "type": "sentence",
      "source": "Establishing a context requires a back and forth over a network connection between initiator and acceptor, typically involving multiple calls to the [`gss_init_sec_context(_:_:_:_:_:_:_:_:_:_:_:_:_:)`](gss_init_sec_context(_:_:_:_:_:_:_:_:_:_:_:_:_:).md) and [`gss_accept_sec_context(_:_:_:_:_:_:_:_:_:_:_:)`](gss_accept_sec_context(_:_:_:_:_:_:_:_:_:_:_:).md) functions.",
      "normalizedSource": "Establishing a context requires a back and forth over a network connection between initiator and acceptor, typically involving multiple calls to the [`gss_init_sec_context(_:_:_:_:_:_:_:_:_:_:_:_:_:)`](gss_init_sec_context(_:_:_:_:_:_:_:_:_:_:_:_:_:).md) and [`gss_accept_sec_context(_:_:_:_:_:_:_:_:_:_:_:)`](gss_accept_sec_context(_:_:_:_:_:_:_:_:_:_:_:).md) functions.",
      "sourceHash": "9568686e8d0f8e1ccc235b82dc9f4d63b158c8af793167bc981f1e14948f1c14",
      "translatable": true,
      "contextBefore": "Discussion",
      "contextAfter": "The `GSS_C_PROT_READY_FLAG` flag, when set by either function as a return flag, indicates that although the context is not yet ready, the forthcoming availability of confidentiality and integrity services is already known and reported by the [`GSS_C_CONF_FLAG`](gss_c_conf_flag.md) and [`GSS_C_INTEG_FLAG`](gss_c_integ_flag.md) flags, respectively.",
      "documentTitle": "GSSCPROTREADYFLAG",
      "framework": "GSS",
      "ko": "",
      "status": "failed",
      "reviewed": false,
      "locked": false
    },
    {
      "id": "seg:paragraph:discussion:0008:0002",
      "blockId": "paragraph:discussion:0008",
      "type": "sentence",
      "source": "The `GSS_C_PROT_READY_FLAG` flag, when set by either function as a return flag, indicates that although the context is not yet ready, the forthcoming availability of confidentiality and integrity services is already known and reported by the [`GSS_C_CONF_FLAG`](gss_c_conf_flag.md) and [`GSS_C_INTEG_FLAG`](gss_c_integ_flag.md) flags, respectively.",
      "normalizedSource": "The `GSS_C_PROT_READY_FLAG` flag, when set by either function as a return flag, indicates that although the context is not yet ready, the forthcoming availability of confidentiality and integrity services is already known and reported by the [`GSS_C_CONF_FLAG`](gss_c_conf_flag.md) and [`GSS_C_INTEG_FLAG`](gss_c_integ_flag.md) flags, respectively.",
      "sourceHash": "6751d547685b1f6922c1d17eeea7746b1a09aa58838c5cac42f658977306f450",
      "translatable": true,
      "contextBefore": "Establishing a context requires a back and forth over a network connection between initiator and acceptor, typically involving multiple calls to the [`gss_init_sec_context(_:_:_:_:_:_:_:_:_:_:_:_:_:)`](gss_init_sec_context(_:_:_:_:_:_:_:_:_:_:_:_:_:).md) and [`gss_accept_sec_context(_:_:_:_:_:_:_:_:_:_:_:)`](gss_accept_sec_context(_:_:_:_:_:_:_:_:_:_:_:).md) functions.",
      "contextAfter": "This allows you to begin using the various protection functions if reported as available, without waiting for the context to complete.",
